    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d151">

                <pb facs="0132" n="124" xml:id="pg124"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">751G.94/117</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Chief of the
                        Division of Far Eastern Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Hamilton</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-09-18">September 18, 1940</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Mr. Butler, Counselor of the British Embassy, telephoned and referred to the
                    Department’s <hi rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> of September 16, relating
                    to the British Embassy’s <hi rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> of September
                    12. Mr. Butler said that the observations made by the British Ambassador at
                    Tokyo had apparently not caused the British Government to alter its view and he
                    read to me a telegram which the British Foreign Office had sent to Tokyo in
                    reply to the British Ambassador’s telegram. In its telegram the British Foreign
                    Office pointed out that it realized that the Japanese reply might be as the
                    British Ambassador had suggested, but that it was important that the British
                    Government’s view be expressed to the Japanese Government.</p>
                <p>I thanked Mr. Butler for communicating this information and said that in the
                    light thereof we would give renewed study to the matter and would expect to get
                    in touch with the Embassy again.</p>
                <closer><signed>M[<hi rendition="#small-caps">axwell</hi>] M. H[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">amilton</hi>]</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
